From bf79835e4ab5f375c3abd8ffd0bc214b769b4093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:31:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(streaming): hide namespaced think tags and runaway tool
 closers; cap output tokens

Treat namespaced (e.g. `think:think`) and orphan reasoning closers as reasoning
regions across the shared TagFilter, the batch strip and the draft presenters;
hide XML `function`/`function_calls` tool markup from every live surface
including Markdown code fences; keep replies that only quote XML function
markup; replace (don't append) a draft snapshot that rewrites.

On the provider side, cap OpenAI-compatible reasoning requests via
`max_completion_tokens` (including endpoints with no configured effort), detect
the `</function_calls>` runaway closer run, and stop reasoning content from
being duplicated across the reasoning and content fields.
---
